{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function getLoadSubsetDemandKey(options): DemandKey | undefined;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/query/ir-stable-identity.ts#L103","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/db/src/query/ir-stable-identity.ts:103"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the exact semantic identity of a loadSubset request."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Abort signals and subscriptions are owners of a request, not part of the\nrequested data, and therefore do not affect the key. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"refetch"},{"type":"text","value":" controls\nwhether to start another acquisition attempt for that data and likewise does\nnot affect identity. A demand generation scopes one asynchronous attempt\nrather than the data it requests. Code that rejects stale work compares this\nkey alongside its generation; query-db uses the key alone so equivalent data\ndemands can reuse one cache entry across generations."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/LoadSubsetOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LoadSubsetOptions"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/DemandKey.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DemandKey"}]},{"type":"text","value":" | "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"options","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction getLoadSubsetDemandKey(options): DemandKey | undefined;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/query/ir-stable-identity.ts:103](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/query/ir-stable-identity.ts#L103)\n\nReturns the exact semantic identity of a loadSubset request.\n\nAbort signals and subscriptions are owners of a request, not part of the\nrequested data, and therefore do not affect the key. `refetch` controls\nwhether to start another acquisition attempt for that data and likewise does\nnot affect identity. A demand generation scopes one asynchronous attempt\nrather than the data it requests. Code that rejects stale work compares this\nkey alongside its generation; query-db uses the key alone so equivalent data\ndemands can reuse one cache entry across generations.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### options\n\n[`LoadSubsetOptions`](../type-aliases/LoadSubsetOptions.md)\n\n## Returns\n\n[`DemandKey`](../type-aliases/DemandKey.md) \\| `undefined`\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: getLoadSubsetDemandKey\ntitle: getLoadSubsetDemandKey\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction getLoadSubsetDemandKey(options): DemandKey | undefined;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/db/src/query/ir-stable-identity.ts:103](https://github.com/TanStack/db/blob/main/packages/db/src/query/ir-stable-identity.ts#L103)\n\nReturns the exact semantic identity of a loadSubset request.\n\nAbort signals and subscriptions are owners of a request, not part of the\nrequested data, and therefore do not affect the key. `refetch` controls\nwhether to start another acquisition attempt for that data and likewise does\nnot affect identity. A demand generation scopes one asynchronous attempt\nrather than the data it requests. Code that rejects stale work compares this\nkey alongside its generation; query-db uses the key alone so equivalent data\ndemands can reuse one cache entry across generations.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### options\n\n[`LoadSubsetOptions`](../type-aliases/LoadSubsetOptions.md)\n\n## Returns\n\n[`DemandKey`](../type-aliases/DemandKey.md) \\| `undefined`\n"}
